<title>FRANCE: Millon cool on any Aerospatiale buy of Thomson-CSF.</title>
<headline>Millon cool on any Aerospatiale buy of Thomson-CSF.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defence minister Charles Millon said he did not believe proposed merger partners Aerospatiale and Dassault Aviation should bid for state-controlled defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>In an interview with the newspaper Les Echos, Millon said, &quot;Does asking a public sector company to bid for another public company appear to you to be the best solution for a privatisation? I don't think so.&quot;</p>
<p>French newspapers have reported that the merged Aerospatiale/Dassault group could bid for Thomson-CSF, to speed up industrial restructuring and boost vertical integration.</p>
</text>
